rk:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">index.html</span> file to incorporate the following enhancements while maintaining the existing functionality (12-level spiral galaxy, bubble shooter, Vim puzzles, skill detection, mazes, and flight controls). The changes will focus on:</p>
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Lowering Sound Volume</strong>: Adjust the volume of all audio files (<span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">pop.wav</span>, <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">background.wav</span>, <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">level_complete.wav</span>, <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">error.wav</span>) to a quieter level.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Flight Mode Indicator</strong>: Add a UI element showing "Flight Mode" or "Insert Mode (press Escape to return to Flight Mode)" at the bottom center of the screen.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Level Selection Visuals</strong>: Add triangles pointing toward a level when the camera is close, and a halo (ring) around the selected level.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Level Selection Label</strong>: Display "Type i to initiate planetary landing sequence" at the bottom when a level is selectable.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Mode Switching</strong>: Allow both <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">i</span> and <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">space</span> to enter "Insert Mode" (minigame mode) for the selected level, with <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">Escape</span> to return to Flight Mode.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">These enhancements will improve user feedback and align the gameâ€™s controls with Vimâ€™s modal interface (Flight Mode akin to command mode, Insert Mode for minigames). The script remains self-contained, uses solid colors (no textures), and relies on local vendor files (<span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">three.min.js</span>, <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">OrbitControls.js</span>, <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">codemirror.min.js</span>, <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">codemirror.css</span>, <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">vim.min.js</span>) and sound files from <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">generate_assets.py</span>.</p>
